@startuml
title Data flow between RP2354 and FPGA

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 105

control "RP2354 application" as App
control "RP2354 BSP / GPIO" as MCU
participant "FPGA configuration logic" as Config
participant "FPGA runtime SPI engine" as SPI
collections "FPGA register file" as Regs
participant "LED, button, tick counter, GPO0" as Logic
boundary "CDONE / STATUS pins" as Pins

group Configuration data - MCU to FPGA only
  App -> MCU : BSP_FpgaInit()
  MCU -> Config : Hold configuration CS low
  MCU -> Config : Stream embedded bitstream, MSB first, at 8 MHz
  MCU -> Config : Add trailing clocks until CDONE
  Config -> Pins : Assert CDONE after configuration completes
  Pins --> MCU : Dedicated level, independent of runtime SDIO
end

group Runtime register write - MCU to FPGA
  App -> MCU : BSP_FpgaWriteRegister(address, value)
  MCU -> SPI : CS low
  MCU -> SPI : SDIO: command 0x02
  MCU -> SPI : SDIO: 8-bit register address
  MCU -> SPI : SDIO: 8-bit data value
  SPI -> Regs : Pulse reg_write(address, value)
  Regs -> Logic : Update LED, GPO0, acknowledgements or capture state
  MCU -> SPI : CS high; release SDIO to input
end

group Runtime register read - request MCU to FPGA, result FPGA to MCU
  App -> MCU : BSP_FpgaReadRegister(address)
  MCU -> SPI : CS low
  MCU -> SPI : SDIO: command 0x03
  MCU -> SPI : SDIO: 8-bit register address
  MCU -> MCU : Release SDIO on final address bit while SCK is high
  SPI -> Regs : Select address through combinational readback mux
  Regs --> SPI : One 8-bit value
  SPI --> MCU : Enable SDIO after falling edge; return byte MSB first
  MCU -> SPI : CS high; leave SDIO released
  MCU --> App : Register value
end

group Ping - FPGA identity to MCU without an address byte
  App -> MCU : BSP_FpgaPing()
  MCU -> SPI : CS low; SDIO command 0x9F; then release SDIO
  SPI -> Regs : Select design ID
  Regs --> SPI : 0xB8
  SPI --> MCU : Return ID byte
  MCU -> SPI : CS high
  MCU --> App : Design ID
end

group Reset command - MCU to FPGA register state
  App -> MCU : BSP_FpgaReset()
  MCU -> SPI : CS low; SDIO command 0x7F; CS high
  SPI -> Regs : Pulse reset_regs
  Regs -> Logic : Restore register defaults; GPO0 low; dim-blue LED
  note over Regs, Logic
    The free-running tick counter is not reset by this command.
    A full FPGA reconfiguration resets the whole design.
  end note
end

group Independent and transduced FPGA-to-MCU data paths
  Pins --> MCU : CDONE configuration state and STATUS input
  Logic -> Regs : Debounced SW1 level, sticky event and press count
  Logic -> Regs : Latched 32-bit tick snapshot as four bytes
  MCU -> SPI : Clock explicit reads for those registers
  SPI --> MCU : Return one byte per read
end

note over MCU, SPI
  Runtime link: CS=RP2354 GPIO1, SCK=GPIO2, half-duplex SDIO=GPIO3.
  The MCU owns CS and SCK. SDIO direction changes only for read replies.
end note

@enduml
